WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.548 --> 00:00:19.458
"Ahh!" yelled when the masked figure jumped in front of them.

2
00:00:20.438 --> 00:00:21.279
Henry gasped.

3
00:00:22.019 --> 00:00:23.340
Maggie and Cole jumped back.

4
00:00:25.541 --> 00:00:27.222
But they were startled for only a second.

5
00:00:28.123 --> 00:00:30.224
The figure was just a kid in a pirate mask.

6
00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:34.865
"Sorry I scared you," the kid said, pulling off his mask.

7
00:00:35.805 --> 00:00:36.565
William grinned.

8
00:00:36.585 --> 00:00:39.686
"This is Luke," he told Henry and the others.

9
00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:41.987
"He's a friend from my old school."

10
00:00:42.007 --> 00:00:46.748
"You must like pirates as much as Nathan does," Henry said.

11
00:00:47.649 --> 00:00:48.769
Luke nodded eagerly.

12
00:00:48.789 --> 00:00:51.410
"That's one reason I like coming here.

13
00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:53.890
I love exploring Pirate Beach!"

14
00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:56.431
"Pirate Beach?"

15
00:00:56.931 --> 00:00:57.751
Nathan echoed.

16
00:00:57.771 --> 00:00:59.792
"That's what this place is called?"

17
00:01:00.668 --> 00:01:01.709
Anna rolled her eyes.

18
00:01:01.729 --> 00:01:04.371
"It's named after some stupid legend."

19
00:01:04.391 --> 00:01:07.273
"The legend isn't stupid," Luke said.

20
00:01:07.293 --> 00:01:09.895
"Pirates used to land their ships here all the time.

21
00:01:11.316 --> 00:01:13.397
Some people think they hid their treasure on this beach."

22
00:01:14.418 --> 00:01:16.700
"Wow!" Nathan looked impressed.

23
00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:19.742
"That sounds like something from a pirate movie.

24
00:01:20.722 --> 00:01:23.745
In fact, I just heard about a new movie coming out soon.

25
00:01:24.505 --> 00:01:28.328
It's called Revenge of the Pirate's Ghost," he added.

26
00:01:29.476 --> 00:01:31.057
"I'm dying to see it!"

27
00:01:31.077 --> 00:01:33.299
"Me too," Luke said.

28
00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.441
Just then William's parents hurried out of the house.

29
00:01:36.461 --> 00:01:40.864
"Welcome!" William's mother said.

30
00:01:40.884 --> 00:01:45.528
"We have an exciting weekend planned for you," added William's father.

31
00:01:45.548 --> 00:01:49.050
"How would you like to search for pirate booty?"

32
00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:51.812
"Booty?" Maggie said.

33
00:01:51.832 --> 00:01:53.253
"What's that?"

34
00:01:53.273 --> 00:01:57.096
"Booty is what pirates call treasure," Luke explained.

35
00:01:57.964 --> 00:01:59.305
He turned to William's parents.

36
00:01:59.325 --> 00:02:01.707
"Is it real pirates' booty?"

37
00:02:02.567 --> 00:02:03.708
William's mother smiled.

38
00:02:03.728 --> 00:02:05.289
"Not exactly.

39
00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:07.711
We've created a treasure hunt for you."

40
00:02:07.731 --> 00:02:10.353
"What?" William blurted out.

41
00:02:10.373 --> 00:02:13.995
"Cool!" Nathan and Luke said at the same time.

42
00:02:14.015 --> 00:02:18.318
"That sounds perfect for Nathan and Luke," said Cole.

43
00:02:19.179 --> 00:02:21.080
"They're both obsessed with pirates!"

44
00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:23.022
"What's the treasure?"

45
00:02:23.462 --> 00:02:24.363
Maggie blurted out.

46
00:02:24.383 --> 00:02:26.004
"Is it gold?"

47
00:02:26.868 --> 00:02:28.069
William's mother smiled.

48
00:02:28.089 --> 00:02:31.891
"You'll have to wait to see what the treasure is," she said.

49
00:02:31.911 --> 00:02:35.553
"But here's how the hunt will work: we'll give you a clue.

50
00:02:36.513 --> 00:02:38.775
You'll follow it to find a hidden treasure chest.

51
00:02:39.755 --> 00:02:42.777
Some booty will be hidden inside, along with your next clue."

52
00:02:42.797 --> 00:02:46.799
"At the end of the treasure hunt, you'll find a big surprise!"

53
00:02:47.219 --> 00:02:48.180
her husband finished.

54
00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.981
"Awesome!" Luke pumped his fist.

55
00:02:51.882 --> 00:02:52.822
"Let's get started!"

56
00:02:53.743 --> 00:02:55.184
Everyone else looked excited too.

57
00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:57.641
Well, not everyone.

58
00:02:58.662 --> 00:03:01.743
Henry noticed that William didn't even seem to be paying attention.

59
00:03:02.704 --> 00:03:04.165
He was staring out at the ocean.

60
00:03:04.185 --> 00:03:05.806
"Come on, Henry."

61
00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:07.206
Cole poked him in the arm.

62
00:03:07.226 --> 00:03:09.428
"It's time to find some pirate booty!"

63
00:03:15.751 --> 00:03:20.794
After Henry and his friends dropped their luggage inside the house, William's father handed the clue to Anna.

64
00:03:20.814 --> 00:03:22.675
"Have fun, kids.

65
00:03:23.115 --> 00:03:24.176
We'll see you at lunchtime."

66
00:03:28.304 --> 00:03:30.505
Outside, Nathan took the clue from Anna.

67
00:03:31.205 --> 00:03:32.846
"Let me see that," he said.

68
00:03:32.866 --> 00:03:36.167
"Luke and I are the pirate experts around here.

69
00:03:37.208 --> 00:03:39.509
I bet we can figure out where the first treasure is!"

70
00:03:40.989 --> 00:03:42.250
"Right," Luke agreed.

71
00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:48.092
"I think we should—" "Don't hog the map," Maggie said, snatching the paper away from Nathan.

72
00:03:48.112 --> 00:03:51.894
"Besides, we don't need pirate experts to find treasure.

73
00:03:52.774 --> 00:03:55.155
We need The Lemonade Detectives!"

74
00:03:56.256 --> 00:03:56.756
"The what?"

75
00:03:57.180 --> 00:03:58.221
Anna sounded curious.

76
00:03:59.362 --> 00:04:02.205
Cole started to tell her and Luke about the detective agency.

77
00:04:03.086 --> 00:04:05.929
But Henry was watching Nathan, who was scowling at Maggie.

78
00:04:05.949 --> 00:04:10.514
"You're not the only ones who can figure out clues," Nathan complained.

79
00:04:10.534 --> 00:04:14.258
"And you shouldn't grab stuff out of other people's hands."

80
00:04:14.278 --> 00:04:17.281
"Sorry," Maggie mumbled.

81
00:04:17.741 --> 00:04:19.163
She continued studying the map.

82
00:04:24.388 --> 00:04:27.950
"Doesn't it look like the first chest is hidden near those big pointy rocks?"

83
00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:32.092
Henry looked at the map and then down at the beach where Maggie was pointing.

84
00:04:32.112 --> 00:04:34.253
"I think you're right!

85
00:04:35.233 --> 00:04:36.054
Let's go look."

86
00:04:40.056 --> 00:04:42.937
They all ran down the beach toward the pointy rock formation.

87
00:04:43.337 --> 00:04:46.719
When they got closer, they spotted a man wandering along in the surf.

88
00:04:46.739 --> 00:04:48.360
"Who's that?"

89
00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:49.461
Cole asked.

90
00:04:49.641 --> 00:04:55.105
As the man approached, they could see he had a bristly, reddish-brown beard and twinkling blue eyes.

91
00:04:55.125 --> 00:04:57.887
"I don't know," William said.

92
00:04:57.907 --> 00:05:01.330
"But he shouldn't be here—this is private property."

93
00:05:02.631 --> 00:05:04.413
The stranger had overheard William.

94
00:05:04.433 --> 00:05:08.016
"Private property, hmm?"

95
00:05:08.376 --> 00:05:09.317
he said with a chuckle.

96
00:05:09.337 --> 00:05:15.441
"It's a good thing my ancestor, Captain Roger Redbeard, isn't alive to hear you say that."

97
00:05:16.322 --> 00:05:18.344
"Captain Roger Redbeard?"

98
00:05:18.728 --> 00:05:19.569
Nathan echoed.

99
00:05:19.589 --> 00:05:22.210
"That sounds like a pirate's name."

100
00:05:23.651 --> 00:05:24.731
The man chuckled again.

101
00:05:24.751 --> 00:05:28.053
"That's because he was a pirate.

102
00:05:28.894 --> 00:05:31.175
He's the one Pirate Beach is named after."

103
00:05:32.035 --> 00:05:33.976
"Cool!" Luke exclaimed.

104
00:05:34.417 --> 00:05:37.098
"Does that mean you're the relative of a real pirate?"

105
00:05:38.159 --> 00:05:38.739
"That's right."

106
00:05:39.179 --> 00:05:40.020
The man nodded.

107
00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:41.741
"I'm even named after him.

108
00:05:42.301 --> 00:05:43.302
You can call me Roger."

109
00:05:44.402 --> 00:05:47.424
Henry noticed that Maggie wasn't paying attention to Roger.

110
00:05:48.316 --> 00:05:49.778
She'd hurried ahead of everyone.

111
00:05:50.718 --> 00:05:53.381
She looked at the map again and then back down at the sand.

112
00:05:54.242 --> 00:05:57.285
Then she dropped to her knees and started to dig with her hands.

113
00:05:57.305 --> 00:06:00.327
"I bet the treasure is right around here!"
